  "problem": "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x?$",
  "worked_solution": "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057609/assets/fa13b048e5ca54c7074bbf6ec11421bfd8fb9e1618abd732a5faa1d78372a863.png)",
